WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.577 --> 00:00:02.656
- [Narrator] At Great Big Story,

00:00:02.656 --> 00:00:06.890
we've been playing the
mobile game Clash of Clans.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.985
Our favorite character is the balloon,

00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:10.907
flown by skeleton who drops bombs

00:00:10.907 --> 00:00:12.947
on enemies from above.

00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:14.657
- [Voice On Radio] Welcome everyone to

00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:15.490
Shreveport, Louisiana,

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.784
and the 2017 Red River Balloon Rally.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.806
Over the coming days some of
the best hot air balloonists,

00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:21.846
will be competing in the sky overhead.

00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:23.569
- [Narrator] So we decided
to find someone who

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:26.623
drops things out of balloons in real life.

00:00:26.623 --> 00:00:28.456
And we found this guy.

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:34.811
- My name is Rhett Heartsill,

00:00:34.811 --> 00:00:37.856
and I am a competitive
hot air balloon pilot.

00:00:37.856 --> 00:00:39.834
Competitive hot air ballooning is an

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.284
accuracy competition.

00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:43.570
We have way points to fly into,

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.910
and we drop a marker,

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.774
and it's closest to that
way point is the best score.

00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:51.421
My sister Kate, she
navigates to the targets,

00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:52.936
driving on the ground.

00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:54.240
She reads all the winds with

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.240
a little helium balloon,

00:00:57.297 --> 00:01:00.207
‘cause we're usually coming
in from high altitude.

00:01:00.207 --> 00:01:02.364
And we want to drop
down on the deck because

00:01:02.364 --> 00:01:06.372
you're more accurate with
your throws from 50 feet high

00:01:06.372 --> 00:01:07.955
than 500 feet high.

00:01:18.275 --> 00:01:19.192
Absolutely.

00:01:20.108 --> 00:01:23.427
The X's are only one meter by one meter.

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:27.594
So, a wizard tower would be
pretty simple to run through.

00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:32.267
When you get down, you're
dead center over that X.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:35.093
Your heart starts racing
like you have buck fever,

00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:37.760
and that's what really makes it.

00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:42.766
I was basically born into the sport,

00:01:42.766 --> 00:01:44.642
and when you start that young,

00:01:44.642 --> 00:01:46.728
it's just normal from day one.

00:01:46.728 --> 00:01:50.171
My father's flown since the late ’70's.

00:01:50.171 --> 00:01:53.010
When he bought a balloon, my
parent's didn't have any money,

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.942
but it turned out to be the best thing

00:01:54.942 --> 00:01:56.393
that's ever happened to our family.

00:01:56.393 --> 00:01:58.723
It's a good hobby to bring us together,

00:01:58.723 --> 00:02:02.640
and we hope to continue
this as long as we can.

